# Without this, `COPY apps/x apps/x` etc. copies whatever's locally
# installed on the HOST (Windows node_modules, Windows-native Prisma engine
# binaries under generated/, stale dist/ output) straight into the Linux
# build, silently overwriting what the deps/build stages just installed
# correctly inside the container. That's exactly what caused "Cannot find
# module .../typescript/bin/tsc" and would have caused a matching Prisma
# query-engine mismatch right after.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
generated
**/generated
.turbo
**/.turbo
# TS incremental build cache — tied to host paths/mtimes, so a copy of the
# Windows one makes tsc think a fresh build has nothing to emit (this is
# what caused packages/shared/dist to end up with .d.ts files but no .js).
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.env
**/.env
*.log
